    <string name="tutorial_step_1_title">1. Set up a games folder</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_1_body">Open your phone’s file app. Create a folder called “Games” — or use the folder you picked before. Downloads/Games is an easy place.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_1_tip">💡 Important: the app does not download games. It only finds and organizes files already on your device.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_step_2_title">2. Put the games in that folder</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_2_body">Copy or move the game files into it. The app accepts .love, .zip, and some .exe files made for LÖVE/Kristal.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_2_tip">✓ Keep the files directly in the selected folder. The app does not look for games inside other folders.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_step_3_title">3. Tap “Select Folder”</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_3_body">In the app, tap “Select Folder”. Then open the folder where you put your games.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_3_tip">📁 If that folder is already selected in the app, you do not need to pick it again. Pull the library down to refresh.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_step_4_title">4. Tap “Use this folder”</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_4_body">In Android’s folder picker, open your games folder and tap “Use this folder”. If another confirmation appears, allow access.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_4_tip">🔒 The app uses this access to read the games in the folder you chose.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_step_5_title">5. Done! Your games will appear</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_5_body">The library loads automatically. Use the Play button to open a game.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step_5_tip">Nothing appeared? Check that the file is .love, .zip, or a compatible .exe, that it is directly in the folder, then pull the list down to refresh.</string>

